    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "which is the conditional probability that a relative of relationship $R$ (say, a full sib) to an affected individual is also affected. Since $\\Pr(A, B) = \\Pr(A \\mid B) \\cdot \\Pr(B)$, it follows that the probability that both relatives are affected is $K_R \\cdot K$. An alternative measure is the relative risk, $\\lambda_R$, the increase in risk given that one relative is affected,",
      "source_page": 537,
      "printed_page": 517,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p033:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
