    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "For example, the population prevalence for type 1 diabetes is 0.4% (K = 0.004), while the probability that a sib has diabetes given it has an affected sib is 6% (K_s = 0.06), giving the relative risk in sibs as $ \\lambda_S = 0.06/0.004 = 15 $ (Davies et al. 1994).",
      "source_page": 537,
      "printed_page": 517,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p033:b11"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        78.0,
