    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "James' identity is completely general and is obtained as follows. Because the $ z_i $ are zero-one indicator variables, $ z_1 \\cdot z_2 = 0 $ unless $ z_1 = z_2 = 1 $, and hence",
      "source_page": 538,
