    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Genetic variances can be estimated using the observed recurrent risks for different sets of relatives (Suarez et al. 1978, Olson 1995). For example, assuming only additive and dominance genetic variance is present and rearranging Equation 16.49a gives",
      "source_page": 538,
      "printed_page": 518,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p034:b13"
      ],
      "bbox": [
