    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Finally, the rate of decrease of $ \\lambda_{R}-1 $ in sets of ever-distant relatives provides a test for epistasis (Risch 1990a). To see this, consider sets of relatives where $ \\Delta_{R}=0 $, so that dominance terms can be ignored. In this case Equation 16.48b can be generalized to",
      "source_page": 538,
      "printed_page": 518,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter16:p034:b20"
